module main

# ==========================================================================
#  Hello, world — as a bare top-level statement.
#
#  A module needs no `def main()` at all: top-level statements in the
#  entry module run directly when the module is executed. See
#  `hello-world-main.cn` for the equivalent written with an explicit
#  `main` function.
#
#  Run it: kira demo/hello-world.cn
# ==========================================================================

println("hello world!")
